    },
    {
      "text": "Figure 1: Zero/Few-Shot Benchmarks. We scale LLaDA to 8B parameters from scratch and observe",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        243.4967803955078,
        504.0010681152344,
        252.52288818359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "competitive zero/few-shot performance compared with strong autoregressive LLMs [6].",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        254.525390625,
        457.3485412597656,
        263.43194580078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "where x is a sequence of length L, and xi is the i-th token. This paradigm has proven remarkably",
      "bbox": [
        107.64099884033203,
        287.1163635253906,
        504.34356689453125,
        299.6379089355469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "effective [2–5] and has become the foundation of current LLMs. Despite its widespread adoption, a",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        301.6403503417969,
        504.0031433105469,
        310.5469055175781
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "fundamental question remains unanswered: Is the autoregressive paradigm the only path to achieving",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        312.5493469238281,
        504.0016174316406,
        321.4559020996094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the core capabilities of LLMs, such as scalability, in-context learning, and instruction-following?",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        323.54803466796875,
        495.18621826171875,
        332.13580322265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We argue that the answer is not a simple “yes”. The key insight overlooked previously is: It is the",
      "bbox": [
        107.53199768066406,
        339.84735107421875,
        503.9968566894531,
        348.75390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "generative modeling principles (i.e., Eq. (1)), rather than the autoregressive formulation (i.e., Eq.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        350.75634765625,
        505.745361328125,
        359.66290283203125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(2)) itself, that fundamentally underpin the essential properties of LLMs.",
      "bbox": [
        107.6709976196289,
        361.6653747558594,
        397.3734436035156,
        370.5719299316406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In particular, we argue that scalability is primarily a consequence of the interplay between Trans-",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        378.0543518066406,
        505.6539306640625,
        386.9609069824219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "formers [7], model size, data size, and Fisher consistency5 [8] induced by the generative principles",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        385.34735107421875,
        503.9971008300781,
        397.8699035644531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "in Eq. (1), rather than a unique result of the ARMs in Eq. (2). The success of diffusion trans-",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        399.87237548828125,
        505.65374755859375,
        408.7789306640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "formers [9, 10] on visual data [11] supports this claim. Furthermore, the instruction-following and",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        410.7813720703125,
        503.99566650390625,
        419.68792724609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "in-context learning [4] capabilities appear to be intrinsic properties of all conditional generative",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        421.69036865234375,
        504.0010070800781,
        430.596923828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "models on structurally consistent linguistic tasks, rather than exclusive advantages of ARMs. In",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        432.599365234375,
        503.99737548828125,
        441.50592041015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "addition, while ARMs can be interpreted as a lossless data compressor [12, 13], any sufficiently",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        443.50836181640625,
        504.3529357910156,
        452.4149169921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "expressive probabilistic model can achieve similar capabilities [14].",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        454.4173583984375,
        377.65765380859375,
        463.32391357421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "However, certain inherent limitations of LLMs can be directly attributed to their autoregressive nature.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        470.8063659667969,
        505.7394714355469,
        479.7129211425781
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "For instance, the left-to-right generation process restricts their ability to handle reversal reasoning",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        481.7153625488281,
        503.9974365234375,
        490.6219177246094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "tasks [15], highlighting a representative failure in the generalization capabilities of current models.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        492.6243591308594,
        500.9547119140625,
        501.5309143066406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Motivated by these insights, we introduce LLaDA (Large Language Diffusion with mAsking) to inves-",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        509.01336669921875,
        505.6565246582031,
        517.919921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "tigate whether the capabilities exhibited by LLMs can emerge from generative modeling principles",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        519.92236328125,
        504.0043029785156,
        528.8289184570312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "beyond ARMs, thereby addressing the fundamental question posed earlier. In contrast to traditional",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        530.8313598632812,
        504.00311279296875,
        539.7379150390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ARMs, LLaDA leverages a masked diffusion model (MDM) [16–20], which incorporates a forward",
      "bbox": [
        107.64099884033203,
        541.7403564453125,
        503.9977111816406,
        550.6469116210938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "data masking process and trains a mask predictor to approximate its reverse process. This design",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        552.6493530273438,
        503.99749755859375,
        561.555908203125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "enables LLaDA to construct a model distribution with bidirectional dependencies and optimize",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        563.558349609375,
        503.9971923828125,
        572.4649047851562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "a variational lower bound of its log-likelihood, offering a principled and previously unexplored",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        574.4673461914062,
        503.9975280761719,
        583.3739013671875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "perspective on the core capabilities of LLMs discussed above.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        585.3763427734375,
        354.9330749511719,
        594.2828979492188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We adopt the standard pipeline of data preparation, pre-training, supervised fine-tuning (SFT), and",
      "bbox": [
        107.53199768066406,
        601.765380859375,
        504.0035095214844,
        610.6719360351562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "evaluation, scaling LLaDA to an unprecedented language diffusion of size 8B. In particular, LLaDA",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        612.6743774414062,
        504.360595703125,
        621.5809326171875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "8B was pre-trained from scratch on 2.3 trillion tokens using 0.13 million H800 GPU hours, followed",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        623.5833740234375,
        503.9980773925781,
        632.4899291992188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "by SFT on 4.5 million pairs. Across diverse tasks, including language understanding, math, code,",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        634.4923706054688,
        505.24737548828125,
        643.39892578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and Chinese, LLaDA demonstrates the following contributions:",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        645.4013671875,
        360.9004821777344,
        654.3079223632812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "• LLaDA scales effectively to a compute budget of 1023 FLOPs, achieving comparable results to",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        663.682373046875,
        504.0006408691406,
        676.2039184570312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ARM baselines trained on the same data across six tasks, e.g., MMLU and GSM8K.",
      "bbox": [
        116.11000061035156,
        678.2063598632812,
        452.02911376953125,
        687.1129150390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "5It suggests the ability to recover the true data distribution with infinite data, a sufficiently large network and",
      "bbox": [
        120.65299987792969,
        702.1752319335938,
        504.0001525878906,
        711.9737548828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "optimal training.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        713.9207763671875,
        167.77899169921875,
        721.936767578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
